  ],
  "units": "Natural logarithms; labelled subsets; maximal means inclusion-maximal, not maximum.",
  "model_rules": {
    "common": "B_n,m is the exact row/column-cap-two DP count. C_n=ln B_n,2n-ln A000755(n). Forecast ln a=ln B-C_n*w, with deterministic witness/cap/ledger clamps. Known exact rows are calibration records, not predictions.",
    "Q": "w is the piecewise-linear interpolation of [ln B_9,j-ln a_9,j]/C_9 at density j/9, evaluated at m/10. Hindcasts at n use only the n-1 shape.",
    "H": "At fixed h=20-m, regress w_j(h)= [ln B_j,2j-h-ln a_j,2j-h]/C_j on 1 and 1/j for j=6,7,8,9. Evaluate at j=10 and clamp to [0,1]. Rolling hindcasts use up to four preceding boards, j>=4. Where fewer than two valid boards exist, use Q.",
    "maximal": "Use f_m=(m+1)*exp(L_(m+1)-L_m). Approximate F by Binomial(h^2,f_m/h^2), hence M_m=exp(L_m)*(1-f_m/h^2)^(h^2). At h=1 the formula is exact conditional on L. General binomial laws are heuristic, not deduced from mean Freedom.",
    "bands": "For each target, use errors from rolling conditional forecasts of n=6,7,8,9. Q aligns targets by nearest density (round half up); H aligns by h. Halfwidth=t_3(0.9)*sqrt(1.25)*RMS(signed errors), floored at .35 for ln a and .70 for ln(1+M). Truncate to deterministic bounds; special exact transform at m=19. Peak and half-fraction level use a minimum radius of one. These are nominal 80% predictive bands, with no coverage theorem; four correlated board cases cannot establish calibration."
  },
  "scoring": {
